Don't blame me, yonder David started it...

...And once my mind entrains into the rhythm of that song;
It becomes a bit too tempting not to stop and bisk along;
I might wish that it were different but to break the pace feels wrong;
And that do be how it is...

He has sounded forth by bisking how the last man set the seat;
He now knows the so-called "workout" was not an athletic feat;
O be swift thou misconfigurer, retreat, retreat, retreat!
Norvid marches on!

Mine eyes have seen the glory of the coming of the Norv;
He fumes privately at dalliance where the dip machine is stored;
He hath lost a third an hour waiting idle-ly and bored;
His truth is marching on!

You have to kinda stumble into saying the shibboleths wrong, it won't work if you just try to pick fights

